<node id="Mortgage Loan">
  <data key="d0">Mortgage Loan</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">A Mortgage Loan is a financial loan specifically designed for purchasing real estate, where the borrower pledges the property as collateral. This type of loan is secured by the property being financed, meaning that the value of the home or real estate acts as collateral for the loan. Mortgage loans typically involve a structured repayment plan over time, with specific terms regarding payments and potential modifications. Overall, the Mortgage Loan is integral to the real estate market, allowing individuals to acquire homes by financing their purchase through a loan secured by the value of the property.&lt;SEP&gt;A mortgage loan is a loan secured by the collateral of specified real estate property.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-cb64d35f2de347c55b0effa77ac26cf9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0031a6554d7d6f650917d185dca826a6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-60c4c20d8bc6a52cda7d60a42edba754&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4523fa52055965ffd8fb7c7a1badd8bf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-179537b4c45f08e77c69e828197fb96c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1d42271ce6fb4dee8837d86cbc31e6d3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f3f248b6dcc905cb618bc79b5abce479&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1ae377d836631c2c07f6ba5b136cf3ef&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fc2767af1f1c3dce0807f3f719686f1a</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
</node>
