<node id="Warning Letters">
  <data key="d0">Warning Letters</data>
  <data key="d1">event</data>
  <data key="d2">Warning Letters are official communications issued by the Consumer Financial Protection Bureau (CFPB) to inform companies of compliance issues or violations related to consumer protection laws and regulations. These letters serve as formal notifications to entities regarding wrongful practices and notify them of the need for corrective action. The Warning Letters emphasize the importance of addressing any identified violations to ensure adherence to consumer protection standards.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-3d92c5b54eb19d29639251a5d3792069&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d681b3426e4796221cff79ceaa80d06c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9ad37f84c5a37ede2df87edb489e24e3</data>
