<node id="Bureau">
  <data key="d0">Bureau</data>
  <data key="d1">organization</data>
  <data key="d2">The Bureau is a regulatory body that publishes information on settlement services and may issue additional booklets to assist consumers.&lt;SEP&gt;The Bureau is the governmental body responsible for enforcing consumer financial protection laws, including Regulation Z.&lt;SEP&gt;The Bureau refers to the Consumer Financial Protection Bureau (CFPB), which oversees regulations related to consumer finance.&lt;SEP&gt;The Bureau refers to the regulatory authority overseeing the approval and standards for HUD-1 and HUD-1A statements.&lt;SEP&gt;The Bureau refers to an unspecified regulatory body responsible for the Code of Federal Regulations and the Federal Register, ensuring the accuracy of materials presented in its resources.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-202d2f76cd0f9edb21526229f52979b1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bff47fe509e4f4d6bcead3da4fd7d82e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-918cc41243b0ac5553824466f93b99c3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-83b73ab7e1a0712a79396df18f6ec6fd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-98a7596fcdd08dfd4d9aed526d03c3f2</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
</node>
<node id="Consumer Financial Protection Bureau (CFPB)">
  <data key="d0">Consumer Financial Protection Bureau (CFPB)</data>
  <data key="d1">organization</data>
  <data key="d2">The CFPB is an agency of the U.S. government that supervises financial institutions and enforces consumer financial protection laws.&lt;SEP&gt;The CFPB is an agency of the United States government responsible for consumer protection in the financial sector.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-98a7596fcdd08dfd4d9aed526d03c3f2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-202d2f76cd0f9edb21526229f52979b1</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
</node>
<node id="Code of Federal Regulations">
  <data key="d0">Code of Federal Regulations</data>
  <data key="d1">organization</data>
  <data key="d2">The Code of Federal Regulations is a collection of the general and permanent rules published in the Federal Register by the executive departments and agencies of the U.S. federal government.&lt;SEP&gt;The Code of Federal Regulations is an official compilation of the general and permanent rules published in the Federal Register by the executive departments and agencies of the United States federal government.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-bff47fe509e4f4d6bcead3da4fd7d82e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-98a7596fcdd08dfd4d9aed526d03c3f2</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
</node>
<node id="Federal Register">
  <data key="d0">Federal Register</data>
  <data key="d1">organization</data>
  <data key="d2">The Federal Register is a daily publication that communicates federal agency rules, proposed rules, and public notices to the American public.&lt;SEP&gt;The Federal Register is the daily journal of the U.S. government, which publishes proposed and final administrative regulations of federal agencies.&lt;SEP&gt;The Federal Register is the official journal of the U.S. government, where changes to regulations, such as those regarding the HUD number or OMB approval number, can be announced.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-83b73ab7e1a0712a79396df18f6ec6fd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bff47fe509e4f4d6bcead3da4fd7d82e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-98a7596fcdd08dfd4d9aed526d03c3f2</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
</node>
<node id="Bureau of Consumer Financial Protection">
  <data key="d0">Bureau of Consumer Financial Protection</data>
  <data key="d1">organization</data>
  <data key="d2">The Bureau of Consumer Financial Protection is the regulatory body responsible for overseeing and enforcing consumer financial laws, including those concerning mortgage loans and disclosures.&lt;SEP&gt;The Bureau of Consumer Financial Protection, also known as the CFPB, is a regulatory agency focused on protecting consumers in the financial sector.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-1d42271ce6fb4dee8837d86cbc31e6d3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-98a7596fcdd08dfd4d9aed526d03c3f2</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
</node>
<node id="Official Legal Edition">
  <data key="d0">Official Legal Edition</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">The Official Legal Edition refers to the authoritative version of legal documents that should be referenced for accurate legal research.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-98a7596fcdd08dfd4d9aed526d03c3f2</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
</node>
<node id="Material Presented">
  <data key="d0">Material Presented</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">Material presented refers to the information and resources provided by the Bureau that are meant to assist users but may not be official or legally binding.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-98a7596fcdd08dfd4d9aed526d03c3f2</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
</node>
<node id="Office of Civil Rights">
  <data key="d0">Office of Civil Rights</data>
  <data key="d1">organization</data>
  <data key="d2">The Office of Civil Rights is a division within the Bureau that oversees compliance with civil rights laws and promotes equal access to financial services.&lt;SEP&gt;The Office of Civil Rights within the CFPB is tasked with ensuring equal access and non-discrimination in CFPB activities.&lt;SEP&gt;The Office of Civil Rights within the CFPB enforces civil rights laws related to the financial services industry.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-bff47fe509e4f4d6bcead3da4fd7d82e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-25c602269240ff304f98a696cdcd7ce1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-98a7596fcdd08dfd4d9aed526d03c3f2</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
</node>
<node id="§ 1024.10 One-day advance inspection">
  <data key="d0">§ 1024.10 One-day advance inspection</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-daec882166d08546d8f3b9c5cd1cddab</data>
  <data key="d2">The Consumer Financial Protection Bureau requires a one-day advance inspection of HUD-1 statements, ensuring borrowers have time to review and understand their settlement costs.</data>
  <data key="d1">UNKNOWN</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
</node>
