<edge source="RESPA" target="Consumer Financial Protection Bureau">
  <data key="d5">63.0</data>
  <data key="d6">The Consumer Financial Protection Bureau (CFPB) is responsible for enforcing and overseeing the Real Estate Settlement Procedures Act (RESPA) to protect consumers during real estate transactions. The Bureau ensures transparency and safeguards consumer interests in the real estate settlement process by overseeing adherence to RESPA regulations. Through its enforcement of RESPA, the CFPB aims to help homebuyers navigate the complexities of financial transactions related to real estate, ultimately fostering a more secure and informed environment for consumers.</data>
