<edge source="Servicer" target="Force-Placed Insurance">
  <data key="d5">34.0</data>
  <data key="d6">A servicer is responsible for obtaining force-placed insurance when a borrower fails to maintain required insurance coverage.&lt;SEP&gt;The servicer can purchase force-placed insurance on behalf of the borrower if the borrower does not provide appropriate hazard insurance.&lt;SEP&gt;The servicer is responsible for assessing force-placed insurance costs on the borrower when coverage is not verified.&lt;SEP&gt;The servicer is responsible for issuing force-placed insurance if borrowers like Borrower A fail to provide necessary insurance information.</data>
