<edge source="Consumer Financial Protection Bureau" target="Warning Letters">
  <data key="d5">48.0</data>
  <data key="d6">The Consumer Financial Protection Bureau (CFPB) issues Warning Letters as part of its enforcement actions to address compliance deficiencies and advocate for consumer rights. These Warning Letters are a mechanism used by the CFPB to enforce compliance among entities and highlight instances of non-compliance. Through this process, the CFPB aims to protect consumer rights and ensure that businesses adhere to regulations. The issuance of these letters reflects the bureau's commitment to maintaining standards in consumer financial practices.</data>
