<edge source="Consumer Financial Protection Bureau" target="Payments to Harmed Consumers">
  <data key="d5">50.0</data>
  <data key="d6">The Consumer Financial Protection Bureau (CFPB) plays a vital role in facilitating Payments to Harmed Consumers, which is a part of its broader consumer protection efforts. This initiative is designed to ensure that victims of financial misconduct receive the compensation they deserve. The CFPB oversees this program, making sure that it effectively serves as a corrective action to provide restitution for affected individuals. Through these efforts, the CFPB aims to uphold consumer rights and promote accountability within the financial services industry.</data>
  <data key="d7">consumer compensation, regulatory responsibility&lt;SEP&gt;consumer recompense, advocacy&lt;SEP&gt;consumer rights, compensation</data>
